-- title:
--   Γ₀(M')-component fixed by the rescaled level automorphism
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. Let $q$ be a prime, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   The coefficient field and its roots of unity. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $\xi \in L$ be a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity (hypothesis `hξ`), and assume (`hιξ`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. Thus $\xi^{q}$ has order $\ell_g$ and $\xi^{\ell_g}$ has order $q$; both are used below through the unit of $L$ attached to $\xi$.
--
--   The level group and the function field. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ satisfy (`hH₁`) $H_1 = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M' \sqcap \ker\big(\mathrm{ZMod.unitsMap}\big)$, where [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ and the second factor is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$; so $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ (Laurent series over $L$) with (`hK`) $K = \mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L\,\big(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,H_1\big)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of Laurent series, of the rational $q$-expansion function field of level $(q^2M', H_1)$.
--
--   The base ring. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain which is an $L$-algebra with $L$ its fraction field, with $q$ lying in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAq`), and with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ have image the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L\ \mathrm{jq}$ in $L((\mathsf q))$ (`hj`), and $j \neq 0$. Further, $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are assumed invertible in $A$ (`hℓA`, `hM'A`).
--
--   Transport hypotheses for the three level components. Hypothesis `hℓ`: for every $A$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every level-$P$ datum $D = (x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$, if $D$ is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $W$ — that is, $(x_P,y_P)$ satisfies the affine equation of $W$, $(W.\mathrm{preΨ}\,\ell_g)(x_P) = 0$, and $x_Q = x_P$, $y_Q = y_P$ — then $D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$ is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $C \bullet W$. Hypothesis `hM`: for all $p, k$ and $h \in T[X]$, if $h$ satisfies `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (for $p^k = 2$ the two-torsion kernel condition `IsTwoKernel`, otherwise the cyclic generator-kernel conditions on degree, leading coefficient and divisibility of division polynomials) then `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h` satisfies the same condition for $C \bullet W$. Hypothesis `hL`: for all $d, n$, $h \in T[X]$ and $x \in T$, if $h \mid \mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\,W\,\ell_g\,n\,x$ then $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}\,C\,d\,h$ divides $\mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\,(C \bullet W)\,\ell_g\,n\,\big((C.u^{-1})^2(x - C.r)\big)$.
--
--   The group-law and Drinfeld package. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A$-algebras, assumed chord–tangent (`h𝒢`: each $\mathcal{G}\,T\,W\,h_\Delta$ admits a points-evaluation) and origin-normalised (`h𝒢O`: the identity section is cut out by a ring homomorphism from the origin chart killing $x/y$ and $z/y$). Let $\mathcal{T}$ be a level transport for $\mathcal{G}$ at $q$, assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`: the transported $P$- and $Q$-sections agree with the original ones after composing with the maps induced by any graded homomorphism realising a variable change, respectively a coefficient change). Hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` assert that such realising graded homomorphisms exist: for every projective Weierstrass curve over an $A$-algebra and every variable change, resp. every $A$-algebra homomorphism, there is a graded ring homomorphism between the projective-model graded rings whose image ideal dominates the irrelevant ideal of the target and which satisfies `IsVariableChangeHom`, resp. `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   Write $R = \mathrm{rigidDataH1Pow}\,A\,\ell_g\,M'\,q\,\mathrm{h\ell}\,\mathrm{hM}\,\mathrm{hL}\,\mathcal{G}\,\mathcal{T}$ for the resulting rigid Weierstrass datum over $A$: a raw point over an $A$-algebra $T$ consists of a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with a triple $(h, (D, \Pi))$, where $h$ assigns to each prime factor $p$ of $M'$ a polynomial over $T$ satisfying `IsGamma0PowAt` in degree $v_p(M')$, $D$ is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, $\Pi$ is a raw Drinfeld pair of level $q$, and in addition the linking condition `IsGamma1Link` holds: if $\ell_g \in M'.\mathrm{primeFactors}$ then $h(\ell_g)$ divides $\mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\,W\,\ell_g\,(\ell_g^{v_{\ell_g}(M')-1})\,D.x_P$.
--
--   The Tate pin. Let $C_0$ be a variable change over $L((\mathsf q))$ and let $x$ be a raw $R$-point over $K$ satisfying the five clauses of `hx`, in which $(X_{\ell}, Y_{\ell}) = \mathrm{tateToricPoint}\,L\,q\,(\xi^{q})$ denotes the toric point of the Tate curve attached to the $\ell_g$-th root of unity $\xi^{q}$: (i) the coefficients of $C_0$ are pinned by $C_0.u\,\big(2X_\ell + \tfrac16\big) = 2Y_\ell + X_\ell$, $C_0.r = -\tfrac1{12}$, $C_0.s = -\tfrac12$, $C_0.t = \tfrac1{24}$ (constants as Hahn series); (ii) the curve of $x$, pushed to $L((\mathsf q))$, equals $C_0 \bullet \mathrm{tateBase}\,L\,q$; (iii) the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-component $x.\mathrm{level}.2.1$, pushed to $L((\mathsf q))$, equals the $C_0$-variable change of the level-$P$ datum $\langle X_\ell, Y_\ell, X_\ell, Y_\ell\rangle$; (iv) there exist $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ whose images in $L((\mathsf q))$ are the four coordinates of $(\mathrm{cuspData}\,L\,q\,(\xi^{\ell_g})\,[1,0]\,[0,-1]).\mathrm{variableChange}\,C_0$ and such that the sections $\Pi.P$ and $\Pi.Q$ of the Drinfeld component pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`; (v) the $j$-invariant $R.\mathrm{toLevelModuliDatum.jOf}$ of the class of $x$ has image $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,L\,q$ in $L((\mathsf q))$.
--
--   The $\Gamma_0(M')$ pin. Hypothesis `hx6`: for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, writing $k = v_p(M')$, for every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $f : L \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{k}$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the polynomial $x.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$, pushed to $L((\mathsf q))$ and then mapped coefficientwise by $f$, equals
--   $$\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}\ \big(C_0 \text{ mapped by } f\big)\ \big(\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,k\big)\ \prod_{\substack{1 \le a \le p^{k}/2 \\ p \nmid a}} \big(X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,q\,(\zeta^{a}))_1\big),$$
--   where $\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,k$ is $1$ if $p^k = 2$ and $\varphi(p^k)/2$ otherwise.
--
--   The level automorphism and the rescaling unit. Let $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lie in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and let $\tau$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q (ξ^{ℓ_g}) q (q^2M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`: for every weight $k$, every pair $f, g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for the subgroup $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $p_g \neq 0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $y \in K$ whose image is the $q$-expansion of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi^{\ell_g}) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$, one has $\iota_*\big(\tau y\big) \cdot \mathrm{qExp}\big(g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}\big) = \mathrm{qExp}\big(f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}\big)$. Let $\mu \in K^\times$ satisfy the cocycle identity `hμ`: with $(X_\ell, Y_\ell)$ as above and $(X'_\ell, Y'_\ell) = \mathrm{tateToricPoint}\,L\,q\,\big((\xi^{q})^{\gamma_{00}}\big)$,
--   $$\mu\,\big(2Y'_\ell + X'_\ell\big)\cdot 2\big(X_\ell + \tfrac1{12}\big) = \big(2Y_\ell + X_\ell\big)\cdot 2\big(X'_\ell + \tfrac1{12}\big)$$
--   in $L((\mathsf q))$, where $\gamma_{00}$ is the $(0,0)$-entry of $\gamma$ read as an integer. Finally, hypothesis `hc` assumes that the curve of $R.\mathrm{act}\,\langle \mu, 0,0,0\rangle\,\big(R.\mathrm{mapRing}\,(\tau\ \text{as an } A\text{-algebra endomorphism of } K)\,x\big)$ equals the curve of $x$.
--
--   Conclusion. Under these hypotheses the $\Gamma_0(M')$-components agree:
--   $$\big(R.\mathrm{act}\,\langle \mu,0,0,0\rangle\,(R.\mathrm{mapRing}\,\tau\,x)\big).\mathrm{level}.1 = x.\mathrm{level}.1 .$$
--   Unfolded, this says that for each prime factor $p$ of $M'$, with $k = v_p(M')$, $d = \mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,k$ and $h_p = x.\mathrm{level}.1\,p \in K[X]$, one has $\mu^{-2d}\cdot (\tau h_p)\big(\mu^{2}X\big) = h_p$, the polynomial $\tau h_p$ being $h_p$ with $\tau$ applied to its coefficients.
--
--   This is the $\Gamma_0(M')$-component step in the construction of the diamond-type action of level automorphisms on the $H_1$-level Weierstrass moduli problem at level $q^2M'$: each component polynomial is the $C_0$-transport of a generator kernel for $\mu_{p^{k}}$, whose roots are the toric abscissae $x(\zeta_{p^k}^a)$ with $p \nmid a$, and the automorphism $\tau$ permutes these roots via $a \mapsto a\gamma_{00}$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_variableChange_act_mapRing_eq_relabel_of_isLevelAutAt_of_level_fst_rigidDataH1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_variableChange_act_mapRing_eq_relabel_of_isLevelAutAt_of_level_fst_rigidDataH1Pow), which assembles the components into an automorphism of the moduli problem.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_Diamond_level_fst_act_mapRing_eq_of_curve_eq_units_of_level_fst_rigidDataH1Pow.lean

